Developed a high-performance text searching application using the KMP (Knuth–Morris–Pratt) algorithm.
Searches for a particular pattern and finds all its occurrences in text.
Uses a prefix/failure table for efficient pattern preprocessing.
Supports searching across multiple text files.
Identifies and displays the positions of matching patterns.
Reduces unnecessary character comparisons and improves searching speed.
Supports advanced techniques such as Z-Function, Rabin-Karp, Dynamic Programming, and Network Flow.
Provides visualization of matching positions and search results.
Performs performance comparison between different algorithms.
Designed for efficient processing of large text datasets.
